# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the W-T1 tau lab (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/tau-lab and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time and the data directory is a path under the
# runner's home. Every value is final. ORDER.txt says where it sits in the window.
# W-T1 (Linear THA-268 tooling, THA-269 the run; tau-on-tt design section 1): Qwen3.8-27B's own greedy answers on agent turns, per seat,
# through the PRODUCTION arithmetic: image tp4-serve-2, profile c2-packed-tp4 with the verify T1/T2 audits ON, plus two arithmetic-neutral
# log flags (QWEN_FAST_PACKED_AUDIT, QWEN_FAST_PHASE_TIMING) in a derived profile. ONE container load for every arm, four cards (TP4):
#   A1 SWE-rebench held-out turns (240), A2 our own Claude Code and Codex turns (96, rig-local data), A3 calibration (the lanes 4 x 4k +
#   4 x 32k prompts, must reproduce v162/v179 within +/-7%), A4 chained synthetic agent sessions (20 x 6, the model's own answers fed
#   back), A5 the thinking-OFF pair of 100 A1 turns. A1, A2 and A4 run thinking ON (the chat template's default, what production agents
#   send); A3 is as the lanes' prompts bake it (off).
# reset first: the window's earlier jobs (T5 is the last that can wedge a board) leave the ring fabric up.
# C2_TAULAB_DATA is rig-local and READ ONLY to the job (the default is kwork64/taulab/data under the runner's home); the results and the
# container's log are written under kwork64/taulab/results/ and never uploaded: the uploaded artifact holds taulab/tau-lab-summary.json,
# aggregates only (the Qwen repo, its logs and artifacts are public). C2_TAULAB_COUNTERS: production's spec-decode counters (a JSON of
# aggregates, positions 1-3 are compared within +/-10%); leave it unset and that check reads NOT_ESTABLISHED.
# C2_TAULAB_DEADLINE: 270 min for the whole run, the container load (about 10 min) included; the driver gives each arm the time left in
# proportion to the design's wall estimates (A1 80, A2 49, A3 3, A4 44, A5 28 min) and keeps 15 min for the stop and the report. A run
# killed mid-way RESUMES when its workflow run is re-run (the results directory is keyed by the run id: the turns already done are
# skipped), and the report reruns over any results directory (c2_tau_lab.py --analyze-only).
# Duration (estimate): 275 min (card time 4.5 h). Stop rule: none (optional); a refusal before the container starts costs nothing.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset taulab
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-2
C2_TAULAB_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
C2_TAULAB_ARMS=A1 A2 A3 A4 A5
C2_TAULAB_DEADLINE=270
C2_TAULAB_IN_FLIGHT=8
